// Stats-based win probability formula.
// Paste into Kibana Dev Tools Console (or the ES|QL tab) to run.
//
// This is a transparent, documented heuristic -- see docs/model.md for the
// reasoning behind the weights. It is NOT a trained ML model.
//
// Formula (before normalization to 0-100%):
//   raw_score = (net_rating * 0.5)
//             + (last_10_win_pct * 30)
//             + (home_court_bonus)   // +5 if this is the home team, else 0
//
// The two teams' raw_scores in a matchup are then converted to a probability
// via a simple logistic-style normalization done in esql/matchup_comparison.esql
// (ES|QL doesn't have a built-in logistic function, so the final
// normalization step happens either in a second ES|QL pass or in the Agent
// Builder tool's post-processing -- see agent_builder/tools/get_stats_prediction.json).

FROM nba_team_stats
| EVAL last_10_win_pct = TO_DOUBLE(last_10_wins) / (TO_DOUBLE(last_10_wins) + TO_DOUBLE(last_10_losses))
| EVAL raw_score = (net_rating * 0.5) + (last_10_win_pct * 30)
| KEEP team, team_abbreviation, season, net_rating, last_10_win_pct, raw_score
| SORT raw_score DESC
